      "page_title": "Loop-Shape Trap & Decision Flow",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Loop-shape trap",
          "text": "With `while (low < high)` never write `high = mid - 1` — you can step **over** the answer. Shrink with ==high = mid== and let low meet high."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Binary Search is a ==family of patterns==, not one problem. Identify the pattern first, then define the search space clearly."
